.TH CAI 1 "" "cai" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cai \- terminal coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cai
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cai
starts the Smith coding agent in the current directory or the directory selected
with
.BR \-C .
It uses ChatGPT authentication from
.I ~/.codex/auth.json
first, then credentials in cai's lockd store if the Codex file is absent, and starts with the
.B gpt-6-luna
model at medium reasoning effort.
The prompt is
.BR "\(dq> \(dq" .
Provider-issued reasoning summaries and assistant text stream through the
terminal renderer in prompt mode. Non-interactive activity is logged through
libpslog; only the final assistant response is rendered on standard output.
.PP
The newest saved session for the workspace resumes automatically.
Sessions are scoped to the canonical workspace directory.
Use
.B \-N
to start a new session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-N , " " \-\-new
Start a new session in the workspace.
.TP
.BR \-n , " " \-\-non-interactive
Run supplied instructions or a goal to completion and exit without reading
from the terminal. Requires at least one
.BR \-i ,
.BR \-g ,
or a review mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " [ID]"
With no ID, list numbered conversations for the current directory and exit.
With an ID, resume that saved session in the current directory.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-new .
.TP
.BR \-C , " " \-\-directory " " DIR
Change to
.I DIR
before opening auth, sessions, or the agent. Relative paths are resolved
from that directory. The default is the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-i , " " \-\-instruction " " TEXT
Submit
.I TEXT
as a prompt after saved conversation replay. Repeat to queue ordered turns;
each prompt starts after the previous turn or goal ends.
.TP
.BR \-g , " " \-\-goal " " TEXT
Create or replace a durable goal with objective
.IR TEXT .
The agent continues until the goal finishes or stops. In interactive mode,
the prompt then remains available; in non-interactive mode cai exits.
.TP
.B \-\-review
Run one isolated review and exit. The default target is uncommitted changes.
With
.BR \-\-base ,
review changes against a reference; with one
.BR \-i ,
use custom review instructions. Review activity and reasoning go to standard
error as pslog records. Validated findings go to standard output unless
.B \-\-out
is specified.
.TP
.B \-\-review-and-fix
Start a new, non-interactive Smith session with a durable goal to invoke the
built-in review subagent, fix actionable findings, verify, and repeat until
the review is clean. There is no default iteration limit. Requires the review
subagent. Errors and stopped goals return a nonzero status.
.TP
.BI \-\-base " REF"
Review against
.I REF
in either review mode.
.TP
.BR \-o , " " \-\-out " " FILE
Write only the final review findings to
.IR FILE .
Standard output remains empty; review activity remains on standard error.
Requires
.BR \-\-review .
.TP
.BR \-T , " " \-\-output-type " " TYPE
Select
.B markdown
(default) or
.B json
for final review findings. Requires
.BR \-\-review .
.TP
.BR \-a , " " \-\-auth-json " " PATH
Import ChatGPT authentication from
.IR PATH .
The default source is
.IR ~/.codex/auth.json .
Otherwise use credentials in the lockd store. Unchanged source files preserve
refreshed stored tokens. Token refresh never changes the source file.
.TP
.B \-\-login
Open the browser login flow, save ChatGPT auth in the cai.auth namespace of
cai's lockd store, and exit. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-auth-json .
.TP
.BR \-l , " " \-\-list
List all conversations across directories and exit. Rows show the ID,
directory, and first prompt, truncated to terminal width or 80 columns.
.TP
.BI \-\-lockd " ENDPOINT"
Select an absolute pouch:///path/to/root or remote http:// or https:// lockd
endpoint. Default: the Pouch root under cai's XDG state directory.
Selected Pouch roots use cai's key, durable sync, indexing, and shared writer
settings. Remote encryption and access policy are managed by the server.
.TP
.BI \-\-lockd-client-pem " FILE"
Enable remote mTLS with a combined client certificate, private key, and CA
PEM bundle. HTTPS verifies server certificates.
.TP
.BI \-\-export " ID"
Export resumable JSONL and Markdown for a conversation and exit. Markdown uses
libcai's existing exporter, including instructions and runtime/goal metadata.
No model requests or tools run during export. Files are plaintext, mode 0600.
.TP
.BI \-\-export-dir " DIR"
Override the export root. Default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/cai/exports, falling back to
~/.local/share/cai/exports.
Each conversation writes ID/ID.jsonl and ID/ID.md beneath this root.
.TP
.BI \-\-import " FILE"
Validate a JSONL export, assign a new ID in the current directory, and exit.
Failed imports are not published in conversation lists.
.TP
.BR \-p , " " \-\-provider " " NAME
Select
.BR chatgpt ,
.BR openai ,
.BR openrouter ,
or
.BR custom .
The default is
.BR chatgpt .
OpenAI reads
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY ;
OpenRouter reads
.BR OPENROUTER_API_KEY .
.TP
.BI \-\-endpoint " URL"
Base URL for the
.B custom
provider. Required with
.BR custom .
.TP
.BI \-\-api-key-env " NAME"
Environment variable containing the custom provider API key. The default is
.BR CAI_API_KEY .
.TP
.BR \-m , " " \-\-model " " ID
Select the model.
ChatGPT and OpenAI default to
.BR gpt-6-luna ;
OpenRouter defaults to
.BR openai/gpt-5.6-luna .
The custom provider requires an explicit model.
.TP
.BR \-r , " " \-\-reasoning-effort " " LEVEL
Set reasoning effort:
.BR none ,
.BR low ,
.BR medium ,
.BR high ,
.BR xhigh ,
or
.BR max .
The default is
.BR medium .
.TP
.BI \-\-reasoning-summary " MODE"
Set provider reasoning summary mode:
.BR none ,
.BR auto ,
.BR concise ,
or
.BR detailed .
The default is
.BR concise .
.TP
.BI \-\-review-model " ID"
Select the model for review children.
.TP
.BI \-\-review-reasoning-effort " LEVEL"
Set reasoning effort for review children.
.TP
.BI \-\-review-reasoning-summary " MODE"
Set reasoning summary mode for review children.
.TP
.BI \-\-agents-md " PATH"
Use the global cai AGENTS.md file at
.I PATH
instead of the default under cai's XDG config directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-config-dir " DIR"
Use
.I DIR
as the global agent configuration directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-skills-dir " DIR"
Use
.I DIR
as the global skills directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-identity " TEXT"
Set the visible agent identity.
.TP
.BR \-I , " " \-\-developer-instructions " " TEXT
Append developer instructions.
.TP
.B \-\-codex-agents-md
Load
.I ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/AGENTS.md
after cai's global AGENTS.md, then discover ancestor AGENTS.md files from the
repository root to the workspace.
.TP
.B \-\-no-image-generation
Disable hosted image generation.
.TP
.B \-\-no-terminal
Disable terminal tools.
.TP
.B \-\-no-review-subagent
Disable the built-in reviewer.
.TP
.BR \-v , " " \-\-verbose
Print runtime events; repeat for event sequence numbers.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH PROMPT COMMANDS
.TP
.B /resume
List saved sessions for the current workspace, newest first.
.TP
.BI /resume " NUMBER"
Load the numbered session from that list and replay saved user prompts and
assistant text without repeating tool side effects.
.TP
.BI /export " [ID]"
Export the active session, or the supplied ID, as JSONL and Markdown.
.TP
.B /new
Start a new session in the current workspace.
.TP
.B /status
Show a Markdown table of provider, model, reasoning, context, and available
cost or quota metrics. For ChatGPT, fetch quota immediately and update the
status line.
.TP
.BR /quit , " " /exit
Exit the agent.
.SH STATUS LINE
The status line shows model and reasoning effort, context used as a percentage,
the workspace, available ChatGPT subscription quota and credits or API cost estimate,
the Git branch when available, and an active goal.
Quota windows are labeled by their returned duration, including weekly-only
accounts and any shorter window returned by the backend. Quota is fetched at
startup and after completed turns, with automatic requests limited to one
attempt every five minutes.
Unavailable values are hidden.
Credits follow the quota windows as
.B crd 43
or
.BR "crd unlimited" ,
when the provider reports them. Balances are rounded to whole numbers here.
Fractional balances appear in
.BR /status .
The message above it shows the provider's concise reasoning summary and the
active turn's elapsed time. Softline supplies its default
.B "! "
prefix to that message. Before a summary arrives it shows
.BR Working .
After the turn settles it shows
.B Worked for
followed by its duration and a local
.I ddhhmm
date-time group (day of month, 24-hour clock, minute). Durations show minutes
and seconds below an hour, hours and minutes below a day, and days, hours, and
minutes thereafter.
.SH LOGGING
All diagnostics and runtime activity use libpslog with the
.B LOG_
environment prefix and JSON output by default. Ordinary prompts, assistant
messages, and reasoning summaries use info level. Conversation records carry
role and prompt_kind fields to distinguish normal prompts, queued turns,
steering, developer instructions, and reasoning summaries. No app field is added.
.PP
In prompt mode, all levels append to the session cache log. Only warning and
error diagnostics are surfaced in the UI. Startup records are moved into the
selected session log; failed startup logs remain in a startup-* file.
.PP
With
.BR \-n ,
.BR \-\-review ,
or
.BR \-\-review-and-fix ,
activity goes to standard error as pslog records. Only the latest top-level
assistant response of the entire invocation goes to standard output. Replay,
reasoning, tool activity, and child reviews are log-only. If a later turn fails
without a reply, the latest available reply is still emitted. Final response
selection uses a private, unlinked file-backed spool; activity logging remains
immediate. Review findings retain their selected Markdown or JSON format;
.B \-\-out
keeps standard output empty. Utility commands retain their normal stdout results.
.PP
Native environment settings include LOG_MODE, LOG_LEVEL, LOG_NO_COLOR,
LOG_FORCE_COLOR, LOG_PALETTE, LOG_VERBOSE_FIELDS, LOG_DISABLE_TIMESTAMP,
LOG_TIME_FORMAT, LOG_UTC, LOG_OUTPUT, and LOG_OUTPUT_FILE_MODE.
LOG_OUTPUT overrides the default sink; default+PATH retains the default sink
and its UI warning notices while adding a file. LOG_LEVEL=warn filters out
ordinary conversation messages.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.codex/auth.json
Preferred ChatGPT authentication file when present.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cai/pouch
Encrypted default Pouch root containing cai.sessions and cai.auth namespaces.
Uses ~/.local/state/cai/pouch when XDG_STATE_HOME is unset.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cai/pouch.key
Plaintext encryption key, mode 0600. Back up this original key with the root;
losing it makes encrypted data unrecoverable. Cai refuses to generate a
replacement for an existing root. Uses ~/.local/state/cai/pouch.key when
XDG_STATE_HOME is unset. The cai state directory must be private (mode 0700).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cai/exports/ID/ID.jsonl
Default resumable conversation export, including checkpoint and journal.
Uses ~/.local/share/cai/exports/ID/ID.jsonl when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset, empty,
or relative.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cai/exports/ID/ID.md
Default Markdown conversation export. Exports are plaintext private files;
the authentication namespace is excluded.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cai/SESSIONID.log
Private session activity log (mode 0600). Uses ~/.cache/cai/SESSIONID.log
when XDG_CACHE_HOME is unset.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cai/AGENTS.md
Default cai global instructions when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set; otherwise
.IR ~/.config/cai/AGENTS.md .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero after a normal exit, a completed non-interactive goal, or a
successful review. Returns two for invalid command-line arguments and one for
startup, runtime, review, or stopped-goal failure.
Provider failures show the available HTTP status, provider code, request ID,
and diagnostic detail. Non-interactive errors are written to standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I README.md
in the installed
.I share/doc/libcai
directory.
